      "content": "these are a solid start. the \"sharp survivor\" vs \"perpetual criminal\" tension for jamal is definitely the kind of grit i'm after.\n\nto make this even more impactful, i want to really lean into the specific social archetypes that make these characters feel lived-in. for the \"institutional\" side, could you expand on the detectives/leadership? maybe one is a veteran white detective who has a very specific \"old school\" way of interacting with the community that borders on being patronizing, and then maybe one more character—perhaps a high-ranking officer from a minority background who is viewed as \"too assimilated\" or a \"token\" by their own community?\n\nand for the \"street\" side, can we get a bit more detail on the community members? i'd love a character who represents that \"unbreakable\" neighborhood spirit—maybe someone older and more established who has a very specific, perhaps more traditional, way of handling conflict. can you give me 4-5 detailed sketches total (maybe 2 institution, 3 street) with names, ethnicities, and those \"social footprint\" descriptions? i'm looking for those subtle, baked-in ways that their race and social standing dictate how they are \"read\" by everyone else in the city.",
